# SEV-1 (round-7 hunt): an edit made while the find bar is open (Ctrl+]
# indents the line four bytes right) left the bar's matches on the old
# offsets. Shift+F3 selected the stale range — here it cut Ω≈ in half —
# and the next typed character spliced it: "reached unreachable code" in
# Document.spliceBy, exit 134. The matches are found again first, so the
# selection is the needle where it now is and typing replaces exactly it.
write f.txt "héllo 世界\n"
open f.txt
type Ω≈ç
key ctrl+f
type Ω≈ç
key ctrl+]
key shift+f3
key esc
type 世
key ctrl+s
expect file f.txt contains "    世héllo 世界"
expect file f.txt lacks "Ω"
